{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>The ornaments (הַפָּאֲרִים).</b> From the root of תִּפְאֶרֶת, by the hand of YD." "<b>And the amulets (וְהַצֲּעָדוֹת).</b> By analogy with אֶזְרוֹעַ, and the proof is from מַאֲצַעְדַת שָׁאוּל (2 Samuel 1:10), for the alef is added like the alef of אֶזְרוֹעַ (Jeremiah 32:21):" "<b>And the veils (וְהַקְּשׁוּרִים).</b> Well known, on the throat:" "<b>And the scent-bottles (וּבָתֵּי הַנֶּפֶשׁ).</b> Upon the chest, which is the house of the soul, for in it is the heart:" "<b>And the amulets (וְהַלְּחָשִׁים).</b> Inscriptions written in gold and silver in the manner of a whisper:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:00.688652664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}